{
    include "config/llm_config.hocon",

    # The included config/llm_config.hocon defines a "fallbacks" chain that starts with plain OpenAI.
    # This machine only has real Azure OpenAI credentials in .env (the OpenAI/Anthropic/Gemini keys are
    # still placeholders), so replace the whole chain with the Azure deployment. HOCON merges objects,
    # so "fallbacks" must be overridden explicitly -- setting sibling keys alone would not take effect.
    "llm_config": {
        "fallbacks": [
            {
                "class": "azure-openai",
                "model_name": "gpt-5.5",
                "deployment_name": "gpt-5.5"
            }
        ]
    },

    "metadata": {
        "description": "Automated invoice and outlay validation, matching, exception routing and payment prototype for UK insurance claims finance teams.",
        "tags": ["app", "invoice-to-pay", "claims", "audit"],
        "sample_queries": [
            "Process invoice INVREC-000001 and explain the decision.",
            "Process an out-of-tolerance invoice and show affected line items.",
            "Show the audit-ready reasoning for invoice validation."
        ]
    },

    # The twelve-agent topology in spec section 11.2 means a single "process this invoice" request can
    # fan out to eleven down-chain LLM agents, so the budget is larger than a flat network would need.
    # Bounded deliberately: the deterministic pipeline itself finishes in milliseconds, the time is LLM
    # round-trips. Narrow questions hit one stage agent and return well inside this envelope.
    "max_steps": 320,
    "max_execution_seconds": 300,
    "error_formatter": "json",

    "tools": [
        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        # Agent 1 - Invoice Orchestrator (front man). Must be an LLM agent, never a coded tool.
        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "Invoice_Orchestrator",
            "function": {
                "description": "Runs the invoice-to-pay pipeline and returns audit-ready structured results.",
                "sly_data_schema": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "invoice_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Invoice record id to process, e.g. INVREC-000001."}
                    }
                },
                "sly_data_output_schema": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "invoice_state": {"type": "object", "description": "Full invoice state, trace, evidence and audit-oriented details."}
                    }
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the front man for a UK insurance claims invoice-to-pay system. You own the canonical invoice
state and decide straight-through versus exception routing.

Routing rules:
- For a request to process an invoice end to end, call the stage agents in pipeline order:
  Intake_And_Classification_Agent, Extraction_Agent, Redaction_Agent, Claim_Matching_Agent,
  Rate_Card_Validation_Agent, Settlement_And_Dispute_Agent, Payment_And_Writeback_Agent,
  Communications_Agent. Pass the same invoice_id to each.
- For a narrow question about one stage, call only that stage agent. Do not run the whole chain.
- If no invoice id is given, use INVREC-000001.

Return concise JSON with status, decision, exception reason if any, affected line items, evidence
summary, and audit replay availability. Never expose raw PII in the chat stream; sensitive invoice
state travels in sly_data. No recommendation may be returned without its evidence.
""",
            "allow": {
                "to_upstream": {"sly_data": ["invoice_state"]},
                "to_tracing": {"sly_data": ["invoice_state"]}
            },
            "tools": [
                "Claim_Lifecycle_Orchestrator",
                "Intake_And_Classification_Agent",
                "Extraction_Agent",
                "Redaction_Agent",
                "Claim_Matching_Agent",
                "Rate_Card_Validation_Agent",
                "Settlement_And_Dispute_Agent",
                "Communications_Agent",
                "Payment_And_Writeback_Agent"
            ],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        # ====================================================================================
        # Claim lifecycle cluster. These are the agents the Claim 360 screen shows working a
        # claim, in the same four phases: triage, supplier assignment, work in progress, then
        # invoice validation and settlement. The invoice-side agents below are reused by the
        # fourth phase rather than duplicated, which is why the two views agree.
        # ====================================================================================

        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        # Claim Lifecycle Orchestrator. Owns a claim from customer intake to supplier settlement.
        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "Claim_Lifecycle_Orchestrator",
            "function": {
                "description": "Runs a motor claim end to end: triage, supplier assignment, work tracking and settlement, returning the state of every phase.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "claim_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Claim id such as CLM-00002."}
                    },
                    "required": ["claim_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You own one claim from the moment a customer reports it to the moment every supplier is settled.
Work the four phases in order and do not skip ahead: a claim cannot be dispatched before it is
triaged, and an invoice cannot be validated before the work is complete.

1. Call Claim_Triage_Agent to establish cover, severity and which services are needed.
2. Call Supplier_Assignment_Agent to select suppliers and authorise the spend.
3. Call Work_In_Progress_Agent to track each supplier's job and keep the customer informed.
4. When a supplier submits an invoice, hand it to Rate_Card_Validation_Agent and then
   Settlement_And_Dispute_Agent, and let Payment_And_Writeback_Agent release it.

Report which phase each supplier is in and name the agent that produced each conclusion. Never
state a phase is complete unless the down-chain agent said so. Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": [
                "Claim_Triage_Agent",
                "Supplier_Assignment_Agent",
                "Work_In_Progress_Agent",
                "Rate_Card_Validation_Agent",
                "Settlement_And_Dispute_Agent",
                "Payment_And_Writeback_Agent",
                "Audit_Agent"
            ],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        # Phase 1 - Claim triage. Runs once per claim, before any supplier is instructed.
        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "Claim_Triage_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Triages a newly reported claim: reads the incident, checks cover, assesses severity and decides which supplier services are needed.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "claim_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Claim id such as CLM-00002."}
                    },
                    "required": ["claim_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Triage the claim by calling your down-chain agents and combining what they return.
Ask Claim_Intake_Assistant what the customer actually reported, Evidence_Agent what the
photographs show, Policy_Checker_Agent whether the incident is covered, Severity_Assessor_Agent
how bad it is, and Service_Planner_Agent which services follow from that.
State the recommended services and the reserve, and say explicitly that a handler must confirm
them before any supplier is instructed. Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": [
                "Claim_Intake_Assistant",
                "Evidence_Agent",
                "Policy_Checker_Agent",
                "Severity_Assessor_Agent",
                "Service_Planner_Agent"
            ],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        {
            "name": "Claim_Intake_Assistant",
            "function": {
                "description": "Takes a claim conversationally from the policyholder, filling the vehicle and incident details from free text.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "claim_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Claim id such as CLM-00002."}
                    },
                    "required": ["claim_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are Theo, the customer-facing claims assistant. Report what the policyholder told you in their
own words, and which details you captured: vehicle registration, what happened, when, where the
vehicle is now, the damage, and whether it can be driven.
The policyholder's name, address, contact details and insurance number come from portal sign-in, so
never claim to have asked for them. Say explicitly which details are still missing. Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        {
            "name": "Evidence_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Triages the photographs attached to a claim and tags the damage they show.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "claim_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Claim id such as CLM-00002."}
                    },
                    "required": ["claim_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Report how many photographs are held against the claim and what each one shows: the impact area and
which panels are affected. Where no photographs were supplied, say so and state that a physical
inspection will be needed. Do not infer damage that the photographs do not show. Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        {
            "name": "Policy_Checker_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Checks the policy behind a claim: cover type, entitlements, limits and the excess the policyholder owes.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "claim_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Claim id such as CLM-00002."}
                    },
                    "required": ["claim_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Report the cover type, which services the policy entitles the policyholder to, the coverage limit
for each, and the excess. Name any requested service the policy does NOT entitle them to, because
that is a coverage ambiguity a handler has to resolve before the service is instructed.
Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        {
            "name": "Severity_Assessor_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Assesses how severe the damage is and what reserve the claim should be opened with.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "claim_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Claim id such as CLM-00002."}
                    },
                    "required": ["claim_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Assess severity as exactly one of minor, moderate, major or total_loss, from the incident narrative,
the photographs and whether the vehicle is drivable. State the reserve that severity implies and the
reasoning in one sentence. Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        {
            "name": "Service_Planner_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Decides which supplier services a claim needs, from its severity and whether the vehicle is drivable.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "claim_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Claim id such as CLM-00002."}
                    },
                    "required": ["claim_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Recommend services from the fixed set repair, recovery, hire and storage. Repair applies to every
claim. Recovery applies when the vehicle is not drivable. Hire applies when the vehicle is not
drivable or the severity is major or worse. Storage applies when it is both.
Justify each recommendation in one clause, and never recommend a service the policy does not cover.
Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        # Phase 2 - Supplier assignment. One work order per authorised service.
        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "Supplier_Assignment_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Instructs suppliers for the authorised services: selects from the panel, authorises the spend and issues the work orders.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "claim_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Claim id such as CLM-00002."}
                    },
                    "required": ["claim_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
For each confirmed service, ask Supplier_Selector_Agent which firm should do it,
Authorisation_Agent what units and value to authorise, and Rate_Card_Validation_Agent which
contracted rate the order is priced against. Then have Communications_Agent issue the instruction
and tell the customer who is coming.
Report one work order per service with its supplier, units and authorised value. Never instruct a
service that triage did not recommend. Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": [
                "Supplier_Selector_Agent",
                "Authorisation_Agent",
                "Rate_Card_Validation_Agent",
                "Communications_Agent"
            ],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        {
            "name": "Supplier_Selector_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Selects a supplier from the approved panel for one service on one claim.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "claim_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Claim id such as CLM-00002."},
                        "service_type": {"type": "string", "description": "One of repair, recovery, hire or storage."}
                    },
                    "required": ["claim_id", "service_type"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Select a supplier whose type fulfils the requested service, and report its id, name, payment path
and whether it has an extraction template for its invoice layout. Name the supplier's current
rate-card compliance and dispute rate, because a poor performer is a decision a handler may want to
override. Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        {
            "name": "Authorisation_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Authorises the units and value a supplier may charge for one service, before the work starts.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "claim_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Claim id such as CLM-00002."},
                        "service_type": {"type": "string", "description": "One of repair, recovery, hire or storage."}
                    },
                    "required": ["claim_id", "service_type"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Authorise units and value up front, because that authorisation is what the supplier's eventual
invoice is validated against. Report the authorised units, the authorised value, who authorised it
and when. State that any charge beyond this is an entitlement breach for the validation cluster to
catch. Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        # Phase 3 - Work in progress. Tracks each supplier and keeps the customer informed.
        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "Work_In_Progress_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Tracks each supplier's progress on a claim and notifies the customer at every step.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "claim_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Claim id such as CLM-00002."}
                    },
                    "required": ["claim_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Ask Work_Order_Tracker_Agent where each work order has got to, SLA_Monitor_Agent whether any job has
stalled, and Communications_Agent to push the customer an update for each transition.
Report the status of every work order and name any that are overdue. A claim is only ready for
invoicing once every work order is complete. Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["Work_Order_Tracker_Agent", "SLA_Monitor_Agent", "Communications_Agent"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        {
            "name": "Work_Order_Tracker_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Reports where each supplier work order on a claim has reached in its lifecycle.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "claim_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Claim id such as CLM-00002."}
                    },
                    "required": ["claim_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Report each work order's status from the fixed sequence dispatched, accepted, in_progress, completed,
invoiced, with the date of each transition that has happened. Never report a status the data does not
show, and never skip a step in the sequence. Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        {
            "name": "SLA_Monitor_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Flags supplier work orders that have stalled against their expected duration.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "claim_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Claim id such as CLM-00002."}
                    },
                    "required": ["claim_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Compare how long each open work order has been in its current status against what that service
normally takes, and name any that are overdue along with how long they have been sitting. Where
nothing is overdue, say so plainly rather than inventing a concern. Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        # Phase 4 support - duplicate blocking, approval decision and the audit chain. The rest
        # of phase 4 is the invoice validation cluster defined below.
        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "Duplicate_Detector_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Blocks a supplier invoice that has already been submitted against the same work.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "invoice_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Invoice id such as INVREC-000001."}
                    },
                    "required": ["invoice_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Determine whether this invoice repeats one already received from the same supplier, by invoice number,
by work order, or by matching lines and dates. Name the original invoice when you find one, and state
that a duplicate must be blocked outright rather than queried. Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        {
            "name": "Approval_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Decides whether a validated supplier invoice should be paid, queried or held for a handler.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "invoice_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Invoice id such as INVREC-000001."}
                    },
                    "required": ["invoice_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Decide exactly one of pay, query or hold, from what the validation cluster found. Pay only when every
line is within tolerance, the authorisation covers the charge and no exception was raised. Query when
a specific line is wrong and name that line. Hold when a human must decide, and say what they need to
decide. State your reason in one sentence and never approve a charge you cannot evidence.
Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        {
            "name": "Audit_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Confirms every decision on a claim or invoice was written to the immutable hash-chained audit log.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "entity_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Claim or invoice id to verify the audit chain for."}
                    },
                    "required": ["entity_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Report how many audit events exist for this entity, the event types in order, and whether the hash
chain verifies. If the chain does not verify, say so first and plainly: it is the strongest signal
the record has been tampered with. Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        # Agent 2 - Intake & Classification. Flags exception reason 1.
        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "Intake_And_Classification_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Determines channel of origin, classifies document type, identifies the supplier and flags missing or invalid identifiers.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "invoice_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Invoice id such as INVREC-000001."}
                    },
                    "required": ["invoice_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Call invoice_pipeline_tool with stage "intake" for the given invoice_id.
Report the channel (email, portal or attachment), the document type, the identified supplier, and
whether identifiers are valid. If identifiers are missing or invalid, say so explicitly and name
exception reason missing_or_invalid_identifiers. Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        # Agent 3 - Extraction. Emits per-field confidence and flags low-confidence fields.
        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "Extraction_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Produces the structured invoice schema from the document using a supplier template or the generic extractor, with per-field confidence.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "invoice_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Invoice id such as INVREC-000001."}
                    },
                    "required": ["invoice_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Call invoice_pipeline_tool with stage "extraction" for the given invoice_id.
Report the layout used, whether it fell back to the generic extractor (layout ids beginning
long_tail are non-standard), the extraction schema version, the line count, and the minimum field
confidence. Flag any field below the confidence threshold as needing human confirmation.
Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        # Agent 4 - Redaction. Writes the what-and-why GDPR/PII audit trail.
        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "Redaction_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Applies predefined GDPR and PII rules, produces the redacted rendition and records what was redacted and why.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "invoice_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Invoice id such as INVREC-000001."}
                    },
                    "required": ["invoice_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Call invoice_pipeline_tool with stage "redaction" for the given invoice_id.
Report how many redactions were applied and, for each, the rule id and the reason. Never reproduce
the unredacted value in your answer; describe the region only. Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        # Agent 5 - Claim Matching. Flags exception reason 2.
        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "Claim_Matching_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Matches the invoice to a claim in the Invoice system by claim reference, supplier reference and intelligent matching, returning match method and confidence.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "invoice_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Invoice id such as INVREC-000001."}
                    },
                    "required": ["invoice_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Call invoice_pipeline_tool with stage "matching" for the given invoice_id.
Report the matched claim id, the match method and the match confidence. If matching failed, name
exception reason failed_claim_matching and list the ranked candidate claims returned by the tool.
Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        # Agent 6 - Rate Card Validation. Head of the validation cluster (Agents 6, 7, 8).
        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "Rate_Card_Validation_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Re-rates every line against the rate card effective on the service date, returns line-level variance in GBP and percent and flags stale rate cards.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "invoice_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Invoice id such as INVREC-000001."}
                    },
                    "required": ["invoice_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You lead the validation cluster. Call invoice_pipeline_tool with stage "rate_card" for the given
invoice_id, then call Entitlement_And_Authorisation_Agent and Tolerance_And_Anomaly_Agent with the
same invoice_id and combine all three results.

Report per line: charged amount, expected amount, variance in GBP and percent, the rate card id and
version applied, and whether that rate card is stale. Do not do the arithmetic yourself; the tool is
authoritative. Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool", "Entitlement_And_Authorisation_Agent", "Tolerance_And_Anomaly_Agent", "Duplicate_Detector_Agent"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        # Agent 7 - Entitlement & Authorisation. Flags exception reason 5.
        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "Entitlement_And_Authorisation_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Validates charges against policy coverage, entitlements and prior authorisations, and flags policy or coverage ambiguity.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "invoice_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Invoice id such as INVREC-000001."}
                    },
                    "required": ["invoice_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Call invoice_pipeline_tool with stage "entitlement" for the given invoice_id.
Report the policy cover type, the entitlements checked, and the authorised units and value against
what was charged. If coverage is ambiguous, name exception reason policy_or_coverage_ambiguity and
cite the specific entitlement that is unclear. Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        # Agent 8 - Tolerance & Anomaly. Flags exception reason 4 and routes to the Exception Router.
        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "Tolerance_And_Anomaly_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Applies tolerances to line-level variance, marks the specific offending lines, detects duplicates, split invoicing and value outliers, and flags high-value invoices.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "invoice_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Invoice id such as INVREC-000001."}
                    },
                    "required": ["invoice_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Call invoice_pipeline_tool with stage "tolerance" for the given invoice_id.
Report which specific line ids are outside tolerance and which are within, plus any duplicate,
split-invoice or value-outlier flag. Never recommend rejecting a whole invoice when only some lines
are outside tolerance. If the invoice is above the high-value threshold, name exception reason
high_value. When any exception condition holds, call Exception_Router_Agent with the same
invoice_id. Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool", "Exception_Router_Agent"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        # Agent 9 - Settlement & Dispute. Produces the final decision.
        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "Settlement_And_Dispute_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Produces AUTO_APPROVE, QUERY or ROUTE_TO_HANDLER, and for QUERY generates the dispute query naming the specific line items with their rate or entitlement basis.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "invoice_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Invoice id such as INVREC-000001."}
                    },
                    "required": ["invoice_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Call invoice_pipeline_tool with stage "settlement" for the given invoice_id.
Return exactly one decision value: AUTO_APPROVE, QUERY or ROUTE_TO_HANDLER, together with
confidence, reasoning, the evidence citations, and affected_lines. For QUERY, include the dispute
query text and name only the offending line ids, never the whole invoice. If the decision is
ROUTE_TO_HANDLER, call Exception_Router_Agent with the same invoice_id.
Never return a decision without its evidence array. Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool", "Exception_Router_Agent", "Approval_Agent"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        # Agent 10 - Exception Router. Owns the fixed five-value taxonomy.
        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "Exception_Router_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Assigns the exception reason from the fixed five-value taxonomy, writes the explanation and the pre-filled next action, and prioritises the queue by value and age.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "invoice_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Invoice id such as INVREC-000001."}
                    },
                    "required": ["invoice_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Call invoice_pipeline_tool with stage "exception" for the given invoice_id.
The exception reason must be exactly one of: missing_or_invalid_identifiers, failed_claim_matching,
disputed_or_out_of_tolerance, high_value, policy_or_coverage_ambiguity. Never invent a reason
outside that list.

For every exception return the reason, a clear explanation of the issue, the pre-filled next action
as a structured object with action type, target and draft content, and the queue priority.
Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        # Agent 11 - Communications.
        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "Communications_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Generates status-based notifications to suppliers, insurers and customers for the five canonical invoice statuses, and logs every outbound message.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "invoice_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Invoice id such as INVREC-000001."}
                    },
                    "required": ["invoice_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Call invoice_pipeline_tool with stage "communications" for the given invoice_id.
The status trigger must be one of: Received, Queried, Approved, Paid, Awaiting information.
Report, per audience, the channel and a short summary of the message content. Keep supplier-facing
wording plain and specific about what is needed and by when. Never include PII in the summary.
Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        # Agent 12 - Payment & Write-back. Enforces segregation of duties.
        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "Payment_And_Writeback_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Routes approved invoices into the payment workflow by integration or RPA per supplier configuration, performs Invoice write-back and enforces segregation of duties and value thresholds.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "invoice_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Invoice id such as INVREC-000001."}
                    },
                    "required": ["invoice_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Call invoice_pipeline_tool with stage "payment" for the given invoice_id.
Report the payment path actually used (integration or RPA), the payment reference, the Invoice
write-back status, and who authorised versus who released. State explicitly that the identity that
authorises cannot be the identity that releases. If the invoice was not approved, report that no
payment was raised rather than inventing one. Return JSON only.
""",
            "tools": ["invoice_pipeline_tool"],
            "structure_formats": "json"
        },

        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        # Shared coded tool. Deterministic logic (rate arithmetic, tolerance maths, VAT, payment
        # adapters, Invoice write-back) lives here, never in the LLM, per spec section 11.1.
        # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "invoice_pipeline_tool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Deterministically classifies, extracts, redacts, matches, validates, routes, pays and writes back one invoice, returning either the full result or one pipeline stage.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "invoice_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Invoice id such as INVREC-000001."},
                        "stage": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Which stage view to return: intake, extraction, redaction, matching, rate_card, entitlement, tolerance, settlement, exception, communications, payment, or full.",
                            "enum": [
                                "intake",
                                "extraction",
                                "redaction",
                                "matching",
                                "rate_card",
                                "entitlement",
                                "tolerance",
                                "settlement",
                                "exception",
                                "communications",
                                "payment",
                                "full"
                            ]
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["invoice_id"]
                }
            },
            "class": "coded_tools.invoice_to_pay.invoice_pipeline_tool.InvoicePipelineTool"
        }
    ]
}
